WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.499
Pay for tools after revenue, not before.

00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:04.999
Free stack first is still the rule.

00:00:04.999 --> 00:00:08.212
This lesson is about free stack vs paid stack.

00:00:08.212 --> 00:00:09.640
Pay tools after revenue.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.139
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:12.139 --> 00:00:15.710
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:21.065
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:21.065 --> 00:00:24.993
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.993 --> 00:00:28.920
Stay practical: audit your stack before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:35.112
Audit your stack: what you use weekly, what is unused, and what you are tempted to buy.

00:00:35.112 --> 00:00:37.184
Remember the objective: audit your stack.

00:00:37.184 --> 00:00:40.983
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:45.128
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:48.927
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:48.927 --> 00:00:53.072
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:53.392 --> 00:00:54.559
Cut vanity tools.

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:57.670
Keep only what touches delivery, outreach, or payment.

